  "description": "To make a strawberry liqueur at home all you need is a few days and some ripe strawberries to a beverage less expensive and more delicious than anything you can find on a store shelf. This recipe pairs strawberries with fresh tarragon but you can use vanilla, basil, or mint.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 3 days 15 min.\n\nNotes: If you're using frozen strawberries, defrost them before use.\nIf you can't find (or don't like) tarragon, other fresh herbs like basil or mint are good substitutes.\nBe sure to strain thoroughly, as little floating bits of strawberry will give your liqueur an off-flavor after just a week or two.",
